WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.6 · Brand, Identity & Image
Brand guidelines

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Short brand guidelines let others apply your brand without you checking every item.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.911
Brand guidelines bring your brand platform, voice and visual identity together in one place, with practical rules and examples, so others can apply the brand without you checking every item.

4
00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:26.911
What a short guide holds

5
00:00:26.911 --> 00:00:36.759
The essentials: Promise, voice and visual rules on one to four pages. For example: A two-page guide for the founders and trainees who run the stall.

6
00:00:36.759 --> 00:00:46.978
Do’s and don’ts: Pictures of right and wrong use, and where the logo goes. For example: Logo top left on posters; never stretched, never on a busy photo.

7
00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:56.826
Templates: Ready-made files for the things you produce most. For example: A price card, a social post and an order form, ready to fill in.

8
00:00:56.826 --> 00:01:08.615
Co-branding rules: Whose logo leads, required acknowledgements and when approval is needed. For example: With the youth centre as partner: their logo beside ours, approval needed for press.

9
00:01:09.015 --> 00:01:09.615
Why it matters

10
00:01:09.615 --> 00:01:14.919
1. Co-founders, volunteers and designers can work without waiting for you.

11
00:01:14.919 --> 00:01:19.852
2. The brand no longer lives only in your head.

12
00:01:19.852 --> 00:01:25.785
3. Partners and funders know the rules before they ask.

13
00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:26.785
Where you will use them

14
00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:31.348
1. Every poster, post, proposal and letter you produce.

15
00:01:31.348 --> 00:01:36.281
2. Briefing designers, volunteers and the first people who join.

16
00:01:36.281 --> 00:01:42.215
3. Your brand governance: one owner and one version date.

17
00:01:42.615 --> 00:01:43.215
What to avoid

18
00:01:43.215 --> 00:01:46.667
A long manual nobody opens.

19
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:51.600
Waiting for the first partner to ask about co-branding.

20
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:58.274
Files scattered across phones and laptops instead of one shared place.

21
00:01:58.874 --> 00:02:00.674
You outline your first guidelines and the templates you need.

22
00:02:00.674 --> 00:02:04.674
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:06.174 --> 00:02:09.274
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
